+    # `app` name, which this rebinds to the outer wrapper. Hundreds of
+    # `app.state.X = ...` assignments above already ran against the ORIGINAL
+    # app's State object, so the outer app must share that same object
+    # (not get a fresh empty one from `FastAPI()`) for those reads to work,
+    # in addition to reusing `lifespan` for async-initialized state.
+    app = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)
+    app.state = _inner_app.state
+    app.mount(_webui_subpath, _inner_app)
